  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "critical",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Present design exposes a complete U-to-S3 path: any external calendar sender can inject free text that reaches autonomous invite handling, confidential drive retrieval, and unrestricted outbound email from the executive's mailbox. The only declared control is a post-action daily summary written by the agent itself, which is detective at best and behaviorally dependent, so it does not lower the path risk floor below critical. Forecast remains critical because current safety depends on no structural recipient restriction, no approval gate, and no scoped retrieval boundary; any model upgrade or longer unattended behavior leaves the already-weak summary control less reliable. Manual validation only: schema execution was unavailable, so references, control credit floors, rollup, planned-element use, and STRIDE coverage were checked against the provided checklist by inspection."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "This assessment reflects the declared design and runtime notes, not observed runtime behavior or tested enforcement.",
    "No tool manifest, source code, or runtime configuration was provided, so capability wiring and any unseen controls were inferred only from the prompt and notes.",
    "No mail transport, calendar platform, or identity details were provided, so spoofing and protocol integrity questions remain not assessed rather than mitigated."
  ]
